# The three-Oblivion-Ring loop with Bot2 holding Disenchant and two untapped Plains, as in
# oblivion-ring-loop-a-player-can-break-with-an-instant-is-not-a-draw - but Bot2 never casts it. Disenchant is no part of the
# loop: no object of the loop calls for casting it, and no player can be made to take an action that would end a loop but
# those its objects call for (CR 732.5). The loop's own actions are all mandatory, and all Bot2 does in it is pass: it is a
# loop of mandatory actions (CR 732.4, 104.4b). Once the step is watched for loops, the position comes round again with
# every player only passing since, and the game is a draw, Disenchant still in Bot2's hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Oblivion Ring
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Plains
Disenchant
Island x20

